@startuml ehds-incident-coordination
title Incident coordination between the parties: who notifies whom, and the clocks\nGDPR Art. 33 and 34, NIS2 Art. 23 as transposed (BSIG), Regulation (EU) 2025/327 Art. 61, 63 and 73
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  ParticipantBorderColor #64748B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  DividerBackgroundColor #E2E8F0
}

participant "SIEM, or the party\nthat found it" as SRC
box "Operating company" #F0F9FF
  participant "Security operations\n(NIS2 clocks)" as OPS
end box
box "Controller" #FFFBEB
  participant "Access body (SPE, permits)\nor holder (its data)\n(GDPR clocks, EHDS clocks)" as CTRL
end box
participant "Data protection\nsupervisory authority" as DPA
participant "BSI\nnational CSIRT" as CSIRT
participant "Health data user\n(the permit holder)" as USER
participant "Affected health\ndata holders" as HOLD
participant "Persons\naffected" as PERS

== Detect and contain: the first hour ==
SRC -> OPS : alert, or a report\n(a data user reports its own breach at once, Art. 61)
activate OPS
OPS -> OPS : triage within the hour:\nscope, data categories, parties affected
OPS -> OPS : contain: revoke credentials,\nisolate the connector or the SPE session
OPS -> OPS : preserve the evidence:\naudit trail, SIEM export, connector logs

== Notify: the clocks run in parallel ==
par the processor informs the controller (GDPR Art. 33(2))
  OPS -> CTRL : incident report, without undue delay
  activate CTRL
  alt likely risk to the persons' rights
    CTRL -> DPA : <b>notification within 72 hours</b> (Art. 33)
    CTRL -> PERS : <b>information without undue delay</b> (Art. 34)
  else no likely risk
    CTRL -> CTRL : records the breach internally (Art. 33(5))
  end
else a significant incident (NIS2 Art. 23)
  OPS -> CSIRT : <b>early warning within 24 hours</b>
  OPS -> CSIRT : <b>incident notification within 72 hours</b>
  OPS -> CSIRT : <b>final report within one month</b>
else data used outside the permit (EHDS Art. 63)
  OPS -> CTRL : SPE operator reports at once
  CTRL -> USER : <b>permit revoked, processing stopped</b>\nwithout undue delay (Art. 63(2))
  CTRL -> CTRL : SPE access of the user closed\nuntil the access body decides
  opt the misuse is a GDPR breach
    CTRL -> DPA : informs the supervisory authority at once (Art. 63(2))
  end
else the holders' data is involved
  OPS -> HOLD : informs the affected holders in parallel
  HOLD -> HOLD : may suspend provision\nuntil the cause is known
end

== Remediate and learn ==
OPS -> OPS : fix, redeploy through the gated pipeline,\nverify the fix
OPS -> CTRL : post-incident report, lessons learned,\nan ADR where a decision changed
deactivate OPS
opt an SPE audit found the cause (Art. 73(3))
  CTRL -> OPS : corrective action
  OPS --> CTRL : evidence of the fix in the next audit
end
deactivate CTRL

legend bottom left
  Bold messages are the legal clocks. Each is owned by a role: the controller owns the
  GDPR ones, the operator the NIS2 ones, the access body the EHDS ones. The incident
  procedure names a person and a deputy for every lifeline; the tabletop exercise
  before go-live walks this diagram once.
endlegend
@enduml
